<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayasthiti Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1395</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayasthiti Malla was a king of the Malla dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a> valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a> from about 1382 to 1395. He reunited the valley after a period of division and is remembered for codifying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> and social rules among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newar-people">Newars</a>. He patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and Newari learning, and his descendants ruled the valley until it was divided among three Malla kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayasthiti-malla.jpg" alt="Jayasthiti Malla" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jayasthimalla_Malla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
